    "_meta": {
        "version": "v1.12.0",
        "description": "Canonical-name + synonym registry (F-78). Keys are stable machine-friendly canonical names (snake_case or PascalCase, ASCII or LSRM-conventional spelling). Values are lists of all human-readable synonyms (English + Russian, formal + informal, with and without diacritics). Documentation and algorithms must use canonical names; raw header tokens get canonicalized via gamma.data.aliases.canonicalize(category, raw). User-approved 2026-05-29; canonical 'Gamma-1C' renamed to 'Gamma-1S' 2026-06-21 (F2-A homoglyph normalization: cyrillic 'Гамма-1С' transliterates to ASCII 'Gamma-1S', NOT 'Gamma-1C' — legacy 'Gamma-1C' kept as alias for backward compatibility).",
        "scope_lock": "Current LSRM .spe pipeline is locked to spectrometric complex 'Gamma-1S' (УДС-ГЦ-63×63 NaI(Tl) detector by Aspect + Lsrm SpectraLine software, internally labeled «Гамма-1С»). Other complexes (AtomSpectra/AtomNano/RadiaCode + their software) are recognized at the alias level but not yet wired into the analysis pipeline — see F-78a.",
        "rules": [
            "Canonical names are immutable — adding new synonyms is safe, renaming a canonical breaks downstream.",
            "Synonyms are matched case-INsensitively and with whitespace+punctuation normalisation.",
            "When multiple canonicals match a raw token, the FIRST in this file wins — order matters. More-specific canonicals (e.g. 'Gamma-1S') come BEFORE generic ones (e.g. 'NaI') so that brand-specific files resolve to the complex name.",
            "Homoglyph rule: cyrillic 'С' (U+0421) and latin 'C' (U+0043) are visually identical. Canonical for «Гамма-1С» is 'Gamma-1S' (ASCII S — transliteration of cyrillic С). Legacy 'Gamma-1C' (ASCII C, historical typo) resolves to the same canonical — see gamma.data.aliases.cyrillic_to_latin_collision()."
        ]
    },
